{
  "_comment": [
    "Equipment: everything a formation physically carries and every production line a factory can run.",
    "category: small_arms | ammunition | armor | artillery | vehicle | consumable | protection | electronics",
    "Production: one factory makes `batch` units every `factory_days` days at 100% line efficiency (7 days = 1 week).",
    "  `cost` is raw resources (resources.json ids) consumed PER UNIT produced. `requires_tech` must be researched (tech_tree.json).",
    "Combat (weapons only): soft_attack / hard_attack per weapon per combat week, firing only while it has ammunition:",
    "  `uses_ammo` + `ammo_per_week` (ammo units per weapon per combat week). Tanks also burn `fuel_per_week` fuel_drums in combat.",
    "  `loss_rate`: fraction of the owner's casualty rate at which this item is destroyed (rifles die with their riflemen; guns survive more).",
    "  `casualty_reduction` (protection): multiplier on casualties taken when every man has one.",
    "hard_attack_bonus / attack_bonus: multiplier bonus when the formation carries at least its establishment share of the item (APFSDS rounds, night vision).",
    "Warships (category warship): `hull` = damage points per ship; losses are rounded stochastically (a ship is sunk or",
    "  it is not). hard_attack is used in naval battles, soft_attack for shore bombardment; `asw`: full effect vs submarines.",
    "Aircraft, aviation_fuel and bombs are drawn directly from the national stockpile by Air Wings (config air).",
    "winter_gear (protection): a formation with a kit for (nearly) every man suffers no frostbite in freezing weather."
  ],
